{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/316017-arcadian-magic-hack","id":316017,"title":"Arcadian Magic (Hack?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-19T00:42:29-08:00","id":316017,"title":"Arcadian Magic (Hack?)","content":"So I am a big fan of <b>Once Upon a Time</b> series. It's about fairy tail characters from &quot;Disney-ish&quot; magical kingdom coming to live as normal people in our world. Basically, it's <b>Fables Light</b>, without mostly animals-made-humans. Most of the time, there aren't really fantastic monsters in the show - but there is fairy tale magic. If characters in series would be low powered changelings - maybe with Kiths Blessing and a dot or two in Contracts - in setting there are sorcerers and witches that brew spells from fairy dust or the ribbon shared by three sisters to change the memories of their loved ones.<br /> <br /> Main question is simple: <b>Is Changeling: The Lost having this kind of magic?</b> Contracts are good for inner powers of Lost, but I here seek the \u201cfreeform\u201d magic. Also, I don\u2019t want to use Awakened system, as this kind of magic I would to be more \u201cillogical\u201d, based mostly on \u201cstory\u201d of characters, probably also their emotions.<br /> <br /> In setting, I suspect, it would be a largely feared Art of the True Fae - they teach it some of they most prospect changelings they want to remade in to their \u201cheirs\u201d. So Losts that practice Arcadian Magic would be much more distrusted by the rest of their kind, \u201cbetraying\u201d them with Others powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T01:30:31-08:00","id":316056,"title":"","content":"Bloop: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/475-wyrd-sorcery\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...5-wyrd-sorcery</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T03:58:06-08:00","id":316112,"title":"","content":"Aside from PenDragon's fun link, Talecrafting can do something like what you want, and it's ridiculously flexible. However, it's also very vague and open-ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T04:26:19-08:00","id":316135,"title":"","content":"I honestly wouldn't go to Talecrafting for this. I'd opt for Goblin Vows. With the right purview, a lenient GM, and a creative concoction of pledge-granted blessing and magic ritual-like task, you can basically invent DIY spells. So long as a fire burns in your hearth, you may breathe flame upon your enemies. You can grant eternall life, but you must remove the subject's heart and destroy their capacity for emotion. Fun little tricks like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}